-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",296,{
[9441]="70037840\n1\tDefeat the White Hand leader\tThe leader of the White Hand Orcs is at the camp north-west of Aldburg. Arcil wants you to defeat the leader of the White Hand Orcs and drive the creatures into disarray.\n2\tTalk to Arcil\tArcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg to the south-east of the White Hand camp. You should return to Arcil and tell him of your victory.\n",
[9442]="70027180\n1\tCollect ox-meat (total: 10)\tDun Oxen can be found throughout Carreglyn. You should hunt the wild oxen for meat to bring to the oppressed inhabitants of Barnavon.\n2\tBring the ox-meat to Gwilum in Barnavon\tGwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon. You should bring the meat you collected to Gwilum for distribution.\n",
[9443]="70007FF5\n1\tTalk to Lynx-mother\030Collect Thistle-mead\tThe mother lynx is at Thrasi's cabin. Thrasi asked you to feed the thistle-mead to the mother lynx.\n2\tTalk to Thrasi\tThrasi is at the hunter's lodge to the north. The mother lynx seems to be completely healed, yet she has returned to Thrasi's side.\n",
[9444]="700351FE\n1\tCollect Orc-heads (total: 6)\030Collect wooden stakes (total: 6)\tA White Hand Orc camp can be found in the eastern Writhendowns -- the same Orcs that followed the giant Núrzum into Scylfig. You should wreak revenge upon the Orcs, collecting their heads to raise as a warning to the enemies of Wildermore.\n2\tPlace the mounted Orc-heads along the road leading to Forlaw (total: 6)\tThe road to Forlaw wraps around the city. You should plant the Orc-heads upon stakes along the road.\n3\tTell Gárwig of your revenge upon the Orcs\tGárwig is in Lornsettle, the Mead Hall of Forlaw. You have delivered some vengeance to the White Hand Orcs, and should now return to Gárwig.\n",
[9445]="70037CB6\n1\tBury fallen horses on the fields of Kingstead (total: 6)\tThe stolen horses can be found among the Orcs near the river Entwash to the south of Entwade. You have discovered slain horses of the Rohirrim of Entwade. In keeping with the Rohirric culture, you should bury them on the fields of Kingstead.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have buried the stolen horses, bringing some honour to their grim end.\n",
[9446]="70028614\n1\tTalk to Dagoras at his camp near Isengard\tDagoras mentioned that he was heading north towards the gates of Isengard. Ondor suggested you rejoin Dagoras.\n",
[9447]="7000F1D5\n1\tHunt the Gauredain until you find Thurmaer's Map\tThe Gauredain can be found in Talvi-mûri, south of Kuru-leiri. Thurmaer has asked you to hunt down the Gauredain until you find the one who stole his map.\n2\tHunt the Gauradan until you find Thurmaer's Map\tThe Gauredain can be found in Talvi-mûri, south of Kuru-leiri. Thurmaer has asked you to hunt down the Gauredain until you find the one who stole his map.\n3\tBring Thurmaer's map to him at Kuru-leiri\tThurmaer is at Kuru-leiri, north of Talvi-mûri. You finally found Thurmaer's map in the possession of one of the Gauradain. You should now return it to him.\n",
[9448]="700655A4\n1\tSearch for Gúrayin\tMalbír has asked you to look for signs of his missing friend, Gúrayin, who was last seen heading north of Zarsatrâd.\n2\tContinue searching for Gúrayin\tWhile searching for Gúrayin in Lower Lebennin's forest, you came across some dwarf-sized footprints. You should continue to follow the footprints and look for signs of Gúrayin.\n3\tInvestigate the fabric scrap\tAt the foot of a snowy mountainside you found a scrap of blue fabric. You should investigate the fabric. The fabric is in Lower Lebennin, north of Zarsatrâd.\n4\tReturn to Malbír\tAs you leaned in to examine the scrap of blue fabric, a terrible beast roared and rushed forward to attack! You are sure that Gúrayin did not survive their encounter with the snow-beast. You should let Malbír know what you found. Malbír is at Zarsatrâd.\n",
[9449]="7006698A\n1\tSearch for Igerna\tVarbris said that Igerna went north to try to find from whence the goblins have been coming. You should search the mountains north of Ritherstad in Pinnath Gelin for any signs of goblins or Igerna.\n2\tSearch the camp for Igerna\tWhilst searching for Igerna, you discovered that goblins have made another camp at the foot of the mountains. You should continue looking for Igerna in the goblin camp, in northern Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tSearch the cave for Igerna\tAt the foot of the mountains, a well-carved cave has been allowing the Ronkrúm goblin tribe access to Pinnath Gelin. You should search the cave for Igerna. The cave is at Krauzhaf, in north-eastern Pinnath Gelin.\n4\tTalk to Igerna\tIgerna is waiting to speak with you in the goblin cave, in north-eastern Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[9450]="700374F8\n1\tLearn of the Troll-handler's plans for the siege\tThe Shatorthum Troll-handler can be found in the heart of Shatorthum in the north-western Westfold. You should defeat the Troll-handler and learn of his plans for the assault.\n2\tLearn of the Troll-handler's plans for the siege\tThe Shatorthum Troll-handler can be found in the heart of Shatorthum in the north-western Westfold. You should defeat the Troll-handler and learn of his plans for the assault.\n3\tRead the siege-orders\tYou have discovered a note on the Shatorthum Troll-handler's corpse. You should read the note.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have stalled a disastrous siege intended to crush Rohan once and for all, hopefully saving many lives.\n",
[9451]="700037F9\n1\tTalk to Otkell\tOtkell is in Gondamon, east down the road from Noglond, and south at the first crossing. Geitir has asked you to inform Otkell in Gondamon about the restoration of the canal.\n",
[9452]="700077E8\n1\tTalk to Watcher Redweed\tWatcher Redweed can be found in Staddle centre. Lolo Wendingway advised you to seek out Watcher Redweed to help out with troubles brewing in the surrounding areas.\n",
[9453]="70028E5A\n1\tDefeat the evil Wizard and take back the \"magical\" items he stole\tIt would seem that Rook has taken a bit of an evil turn now that he sees himself as a fully accomplished Wizard. You should defeat Rook before he tries to hold to any of his promises.\n2\tBring the shiny ball to Envus in Galtrev\tEnvus is in Galtrev, still without her stolen toy ball. You should return the toy ball to Envus, who has been without it long enough.\n",
[9454]="70014829\n1\tSearch for Nykr\tNykr could be anywhere, but it is up to you and Sori to search in the southern tunnels, while the dwarves of other camps search near their own sites. You should search for Nykr in the southern passages of the Silvertine Lodes.\n2\tReturn to Sori with news of Nykr's death\tSori is on the platform in the southern tunnels of the Silvertine Lodes. You should return to Sori with the news that Nykr has been found -- dead.\n",
[9455]="7001C06F\n1\tDefeat Galrîp\tGalrîp leads the trolls at Harloeg, south and east of the Tornstones. Kekkonen made it clear that killing the leader of the trolls would be a great boon. He mentioned that the creature wanders through the woods of Harloeg.\n2\tTalk to Kekkonen at the Tornstones\tKekkonen and the other Earth-kin are at the Tornstones, north and east of Harloeg and south of Ost Guruth. You should return to Kekkonen and tell him of your success.\n",
[9456]="700216C1\n1\tCollect fake Forsaken Ale from the Prancing Pony\tBarliman Butterbur can be found at The Prancing Pony in Bree-town. You should speak with Barliman Butterbur, for he sells Barliman's Best, which shall be brought to Alrek cleverly disguised as Forsaken Ale.\n2\tBring the fake Forsaken Ale to Alrek at Thrasi's Lodge\tAlrek is at Thrasi's Lodge in Ered Luin. You should deliver the fake Forsaken Ale, actually Barliman's Best, to Alrek, for it will confuse him greatly.\n",
[9457]="7000E864\n1\tCollect Forsaken Ale from the Forsaken Inn\tForsaken Ale can be purchased at The Forsaken Inn in the Lone-lands. You should travel to The Forsaken Inn to purchase Forsaken Ale for Alrek, who waits at Thrasi's Lodge for some assistance.\n2\tBring the Forsaken Ale to Alrek\tAlrek is at Thrasi's Lodge in Ered Luin, far to the west of the Lone-lands. Alrek has asked you to collect a Forsaken Ale for him from Anlaf the Forlorn at The Forsaken Inn.\n",
[9458]="7001AB9E\n1\tDefeat all three champions of Dol Guldur at once\tUrcheron, Carchrien, and Durkâr, the champions of Dol Guldur, are in Sâd-en-Dagor, north-east of Helethir, in Dol Guldur. Torist has asked you to defeat all three champions of Dol Guldur in one strike.\n2\tTalk to Torist at Helethir\tTorist is in Helethir, south-west from Dol Guldur. You should return to Torist for your reward.\n",
[9459]="7003EA67\n1\tClear brambles from Fangorn Forest (total: 8)\tBrambles can be found throughout north-eastern Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam has asked you to clear the brambles from Fangorn Forest before planting the seeds of Orofarnë and Carnimírië.\n2\tJourney to the Easeful Mead\tThe Easeful Mead can be found to the north of Derndingle, across the river Entwash. You have cleared the forest of brambles and should now plant the seeds of Orofarnë and Carnimírië as Quickbeam asked.\n3\tPlant Orofarnë's seed in fertile ground\030Plant Carnimírië's seed in fertile ground\tMounds of fertile earth can be found near the Easeful Mead in northern Fangorn Forest. You have arrived at the Easeful Mead with the seeds of Orofarnë and Carnimírië, and should now plant the seeds.\n4\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found in Derndingle in Fangorn Forest. You have cleared the woods of brambles and planted the seeds of Quickbeam's fallen friends.\n",
[9460]="70060583\n1\tFind Cariad outside Tornhad\tCariad will be waiting for you outside of Tornhad, south of the river. You should meet up with him.\n2\tTalk to Lagordal\tIt seems Cariad has not escaped the sharp eyes of the Rangers. You should talk to Lagordal outside Tornhad.\n3\tTalk to Erlys\tWith Cariad captured, the next thing to do would be to notify Erlys. She can be found in the Cuan-lûth Refuge, to the north of Tornhad.\n",
[9461]="7000F495\n1\tTalk to Misty Bolger\tMisty Bolger is north and east of Michel Delving in the town of Bywater. Estmar Bolger has asked that you visit his sister, Misty Bolger, and find out how many fish she caught last week.\n",
[9462]="7001AF8E\n1\tBring the treasure to Addie Wheatley\030Collect Cardolan Treasure\tThe treasure is rumoured in the protection of a wight Lord at the deepest point of Ost Gorthad. Addie Wheatley is at the Dead Man's Perch in the Barrow-downs. Edith Sweetrose wants you to search for the treasure of Cardolan to ease Addie Wheatley's pain over losing her two sons.\n",
[9463]="70033331\n1\tUse the Summoning Horn to call Svanr to your side\tThe Summoning Horn can be found near Svanr at his small camp in northern Nud-melek. You should use the Summoning Horn to call Svanr when you are ready to depart.\n2\tTalk to Svanr once you reach the First Hall (summon him using the horn he gave you)\tThe First Hall can be found at the eastern-most gate of Nud-melek. Svanr can be summoned using the horn he gave you. You should head east with Svanr to finish your pilgrimage through Moria.\n3\tTalk to Svanr at the First Hall\tThe First Hall can be found at the eastern-most gate of Nud-melek. You should head east with Svanr to finish your pilgrimage through Moria.\n",
[9464]="7006B7A5\n1\tReturn to the salt mines\tAmâsu has asked you to attempt to enter the other mine tunnels in the hills north of Iridír. She believes one of them may be the location of the lost library, Dubarâkh.\n2\tCheck the gate on the nearby mine tunnel\tAmâsu believes one of the other mine tunnels may be the location of the lost archive, Dubarâkh. You should check the gates to see if you can get into them.\n3\tCheck the gate across the bridge\tAmâsu believes one of the other mine tunnels may be the location of the lost archive, Dubarâkh. You should check the gates to see if you can get into them.\n4\tEnter the abandoned mine tunnel\tAmâsu believes one of the other mine tunnels may be the location of the lost archive, Dubarâkh. You have found a mine tunnel with a rusted gate that you are able to open. You should enter the tunnel.\n5\tDefeat usan-kûni (total: 8)\030Explore the mine tunnels\tYou have found a mine tunnel with a rusted gate that you were able to open. Inside, dangerous scorpions are present. You should defeat them.\n6\tExamine the wall\tYou have found a mine tunnel with a rusted gate that you were able to open. While exploring the tunnels, you found a wall that struck you as odd.\n7\tTalk to Amâsu\tWhile exploring another salt mine tunnel, you noticed an unusual wall. You should tell Amâsu.\n",
[9465]="7006A955\n1\tCollect sewer-lurker meat (total: 4)\tAhûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. You can find sewer-lurkers throughout Ilmabiri; the Wells.\n2\tFind a good place for the bait\tAhûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. Find a good location in the sewers under the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl to place the bait.\n3\tSummon and defeat Imkhâlam\tAhûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. Place the bait to lure Imkhâlam to you. Imkhâlam is in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\n4\tSummon and defeat Imkhâlam\tAhûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. Place the bait to lure Imkhâlam to you. Imkhâlam is in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\n5\tTalk to Ahûd\tYou have summoned and defeated Imkhâlam the giant crocodile. Return to Ahûd at Kruha-sûrja, the guard post in the northern part of the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[9466]="70046C30\n1\tCollect marrow-root in North Ithilien (total: 10)\tMarrow-root can be found within Aelin Veren and among the stony foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath. Thai-chât has asked you to seek marrow-root in the ruins of Aelin Veren as well as along the Ephel Dúath, as he hopes it can be used to lure his Mûmak out of the lands of North Ithilien.\n2\tFind Lokhu-achi in the wilds of North Ithilien\tLokhu-achi can be found somewhere among the wilds of North Ithilien far to the south-west of Cirith Negen. Thai-chât has asked you to discover the location of his pet Mûmak, Lokhu-achi, before luring him from the lands of Ithilien.\n3\tCrack marrow-root on a stone to the north of Lokhu-achi\tThe Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien. You have discovered Lokhu-achi's location and now should crack marrow-root and smear it on stones to lure this Mûmak to the western reaches of North Ithilien and the Nindalf.\n4\tCrack marrow-root on a stone further north of Lokhu-achi\tThe Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien. Lokhu-achi is now following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.\n5\tCrack marrow-root on a stone further north-west of Lokhu-achi\tThe Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien. Lokhu-achi is still following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.\n6\tCrack marrow-root on a stone further north-west of Lokhu-achi\tThe Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien. Lokhu-achi is still following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.\n7\tCrack marrow-root on a stone in the far marshes of the Nindalf and then coax Lokhu-achi towards the Nindalf\tThe Nindalf can be found in the far north-western reaches of North Ithilien. Lokhu-achi is still following you. You should lead the Mûmak to the edge of the Nindalf.\n8\tTalk to Thai-chât\tThai-chât can be found at Aelin Veren, in central North Ithilien. You have sent Lokhu-achi beyond the lands of Ithilien and should now return to Thai-chât.\n",
[9467]="70009829\n1\tThe treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed: \"On the western shore of mighty Lake Nenuial, Stone paths run to the water from a flat clearing.\" You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.\t\n",
[9468]="70002C68\n1\tFind and speak with Aggy Digweed\tAggy Digweed is at the Trestlespan on the northern edge of town. According to Captain Trotter, Aggy Digweed was the only guard who may be able to shed light on the unfortunate circumstances that have befallen Trestlebridge.\n",
[9469]="70048CA1\n1\tCollect strong vines (total: 10)\tStrong vines can be found in the trees near Seregost. You should collect strong vines.\n2\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be found near Seregost. You should talk to Viznak.\n",
[9470]="7004E6D9\n1\tTalk to Rúni\tRúni can be found at Skarháld. You should talk to Rúni and hear his thoughts on how to track the dragon Etterfang.\n2\tSearch Rúni's belongings\tYou should search Rúni's belongings in Skarháld for any scroll mentioning Etterfang.\n3\tContinue searching Rúni's belongings\tYou should continue searching Rúni's belongings in Skarháld for any scroll mentioning Etterfang.\n4\tBring the moon-letter to Rúni\tYou should bring the scroll to Rúni in Skarháld.\n",
[9471]="70062F21\n1\tSpeak with the Ongbúrz emissary\tYou may seek the blessing of the Ongbúrz clan. All you need do is renounce all other clans.\n",
[9472]="700011CC\n1\tTalk to the gate-keeper of Gath Forthnír\tGath Forthnír is far to the north of Gabilshathûr. Commander Gisur told you that Golodir's army was not completely destroyed, and the Ranger has established a camp in the north, Gath Forthnír.\n",
})
